      "id": 1,
      "text": "Faison was originally called 'Faison's Depot' and was founded in early 1833.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faison%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named for Henry Faison, the original owner of the town site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faison%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Faison Depot station, built in 1888, now houses the Faison Library & Museum and preserves photo albums, diaries, and old school books from the 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.faisonnc.org/faison-history-time-line/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1838, the Wilmington and Raleigh Railroad tracks ran through Faison’s Depot, linking the town to a 161.25‑mile line that was the longest railroad in the world.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.faisonnc.org/faison-history-time-line/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Faison Male Academy, founded in the late 19th century, operated until the early 1900s, reflecting the town’s early commitment to education.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.faisonnc.org/faison-history-time-line/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Faison Depot Museum showcases artifacts and exhibits from the town’s past, highlighting its deep historical roots and charming architecture.",
